// A value-producing `if` takes its first branch's type, and a later branch may
// produce a value of another type that compiled code stores the same way — an
// enum's tag where a t8 was expected. Compiled code read the tag as the t8 and
// printed 1 for `C::Green`; the interpreter prints the variant. Compiled code
// now refuses the program (SKIP) rather than answer differently.
enum C { Red, Green, Blue }
c: bool = false
k: t8 = 0
let y;
y = if c { k } else { C::Green }
print(y)
